# A number spelling that no type of its C99 list holds (the grammar, section 4, #numbers: the forms of ANSI C/C99) is refused where it
# stands, before any execution: the list of an unsuffixed decimal is int, long, llong, and 9223372036854775808 is one beyond the largest
# llong. The builder answers 2; no word, no wrapped value and no other type is made of it.
int: before 1
llong: c 9223372036854775808
before := 2
